.TH FLUXMEDIA 1 "October 2026" "FluxMedia 1.18.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fluxmedia \- cross-platform media portal and processing toolkit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fluxmedia
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIURL\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
FluxMedia is a media manager, automated downloader, and local streaming
gateway with a terminal UI and a web dashboard. It downloads video, audio,
playlists and subtitles via
.BR yt-dlp (1),
post-processes with
.BR ffmpeg (1),
and can share files over the LAN with a password-protected HTTP server
and QR-code access.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-web
Launch the web UI dashboard (also available with \fBW\fR in the main menu).
.TP
.BR \-\-tui
Open the Textual TUI dashboard directly.
.TP
.BR \-\-doctor
Print an environment/dependency diagnostic report.
.TP
.BR \-\-check
Preflight check used by installers (non-interactive).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Launch the interactive console portal:
.B fluxmedia
.TP
Launch the web dashboard:
.B fluxmedia --web
.TP
Open the TUI dashboard:
.B fluxmedia --tui
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/FluxMedia/
User data directory (config.json, history, downloads index, logs).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yt-dlp (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR pipx (1)
